Here is a JavaScript function to remove duplicate values from an array:

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(arr) {
  return arr.filter(item => {
    return item !== arr.filter(item => item !== item).length;
  });
}
```

### Explanation:
This function filters out duplicates by checking if an element is different from the rest of the array. It uses a nested filter to check if the current element is different from the rest of the array.

### Example:
```javascript
const arr = [1, 2, 2, 3, 2, 4];
console.log(removeDuplicates(arr)); // Output: [1, 2, 3, 4]
```

